CORE broken-cprover-smt-backend no-new-smt
main.c
--z3
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ a zero at or after n: FAILURE$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ n is not 3: FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
non-constant value
^VERIFICATION ERROR$
--
When the model leaves a quantified formula unconstrained, Z3 (default tactic)
eliminates the Boolean that names it and returns the quantified formula as its
value on (get-value ...), which cbmc reported as "SMT2 solver returned
non-constant value" and VERIFICATION ERROR. Problems with quantifiers are
now solved with Z3 tactic.default_tactic=smt, which keeps those Booleans.
